on Wednesday news broke that Steven  twitch boss died from a self-inflicted  gunshot wound and now ET has learned  that the former Ellen Show DJ left a  note behind indicating that he couldn't  go on  ET confirmed that on Monday twitch  checked into the Oak Tree Inn in Encino  California a motel less than a mile from  his home when he didn't check out at  11AM on Tuesday Morning housekeeping and  management knocked on his door  repeatedly before opening the door and  calling the police twitch's death was  also confirmed by his wife Allison  holker in a statement to ET where she  reflected on her husband's Life and  Legacy writing that he lit up every room  he stepped into quote he valued family  friends and Community Above All Else and  leading with love and light was  everything to him I have the sweetest  husband in the entire world Allison  concluded her emotional statement with  one final message we love you we miss  you and I will always Save the Last  Dance For You I feel like we connect a  lot through dance so it's just sometimes  fun like to have a partner in life that  I can also dance with you know it just  makes every single day so fun now Azores  close to the fan family tells E.T  Allison is surrounded by a lot of  friends and family and is trying to cope  as best she can for their kids Allison  and twitch have two children together  six-year-old son Maddox and  three-year-old daughter ziya twitch is  also dad to holker's 14 year old  daughter Wesley from a previous  relationship we love the Full House and  also just like family man like honestly  they're my favorite they're my favorite  people you know what I mean following  news of his death reports surface that  the family was in bad shape financially  but our source says any rumors about  their finances being out of order are  completely false meanwhile twitch's  famous friends continue grieving his  loss he's never going to be out of my  life he's he's always a part of my life  I love the family that we've gone to and  um something that I always remember is  that you gave me a place  or I could just be myself Ellen  DeGeneres shared an emotional clip to  Instagram Thursday writing that she  wanted to remember all the love and  laughter they shared  that's absolutely  which served as the house DJ on The  Ellen Degeneres Show from 2014 until the  series ended earlier this year he even  added the title executive producer to  his name I'm still in a lot of shock  um my daughter is really close with  Wesley his daughter and our kids went to  school together and he and I went to  college together and um  yeah it's a lot so  ET was with boss's longtime friend Jody  Sweetin shortly after the tragic news  broke he's such a talent and such an  amazing warm wonderful heart and uh yeah  he will be he will be greatly missed  [Music]
 

